      "There are two great forms of worship in Scripture. The first is gathered worship — the whole people of God together, around Word and sacrament. Hebrews 10:25 commands the gathering, and the early Church practiced it from day one (Acts 2:42-47). The reasons are practical and theological. The Body is a body — different parts, mutual ministry, shared sacraments. Solo Christianity is a contradiction in terms. There is no substitute for the local church physically gathered.",
